  "description": "This dataset contains magnetoencephalography (MEG) recordings from 12 participants listening to continuous narrative speech, along with an empty-room recording, stimulus files, and derivatives. The dataset was collected to investigate how listeners integrate local and unified predictive linguistic models during speech perception, examining neural signatures of context-dependent processing across the superior temporal lobes.",
  "methods_description": "MEG data were recorded while participants listened to continuous narrative speech and stored in FIFF format, processed and converted to BIDS using MNE-Python and MNE-BIDS. MRI data are not subject-specific anatomical scans but derived from the fsaverage template using subject-specific scaling parameters.",
